{
    "test_name": "MOB.740_AssetLookup_Work_History",
    "details": {
        "name": "MOB.740_AssetLookup_Work_History",
        "type": "browser",
        "status": "paused",
        "message": "`MOB.740` **The `Work History` tab's CONTENTS \u2014 `WorkLookupDetails`, the four-tab work panel.**\n- `MOB.700` asserts the tab *exists*; **nothing had ever opened it**. This covers what is\n  behind it: the history list, and the modal panel a history row opens.\n- \u2b50 **Covers two screens at once.** `WorkLookupDetails` is also the map's `WorkCard`\n  (`Map/Card/WorkCard.tsx:29`) \u2014 the `MOB.710` leverage argument, applied deliberately.\n  It is also the **only place an `Attachments` tab renders on a read path**.\n- \u26a0\ufe0f **The path is a MODAL, not a route** \u2014 a history row sets `selectedId` and\n  `WorkHistory.tsx:198` opens it. Every tab locator is **scoped to\n  `.mantine-Modal-content`**: the accordion's own six-tab strip stays mounted behind the\n  modal, so an unscoped `[role=tab]` matches ten elements (trap 3).\n- \ud83d\uded1 **`onClose` is a no-op** (`() => {}`, `withCloseButton: false`), so **Escape and the\n  overlay click do nothing here** \u2014 unlike `MOB.720`'s picker. The only dismissal is the\n  inner `CloseButton`, and it is `alwaysExecute`.\n- **The row guard is critical, not an exclusive-or**: the panel IS the subject, so a run\n  that saw `No History Found` has proven nothing. A failure there means the fixture lost\n  its history, and is named to read that way.\n- \ud83d\uded1 **READ-ONLY**, and it deliberately does not touch the `StructuredQuery` bar above the\n  list \u2014 `useFilterState` persists, and a stray filter would change every later run.",
        "tags": [
            "Mobile",
            "env:dev",
            "Asset Lookup",
            "Work History",
            "read-only"
        ],
        "locations": [
            "gcp:us-west2"
        ],
